    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`vim.pack`'s update buffer behaves badly when restoring a session (for example, with `:restart`). To reproduce:\n- `nvim --clean`\n- `:packupdate`\n- `:restart`\n\n<img width=\"865\" height=\"561\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/14bcc2c9-dec7-43e8-8d0b-4db332c4b71a\" />\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEither:\n- Remove `:packupdate` windows when session file is loaded.\n- Repopulate the buffer so it's seamless. (what I'd recommend doing, but it would probably involve needing to change the buffer name to not include the buffer number)\n\nRelated: #1180 #40336",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't think this is a `vim.pack` issue per se, but how `:restart` (and session restore in general) handles scratch buffers. The same behavior can be observed, for example, with `:checkhealth` buffer.\n\nAnd #40336 is indeed related as the behavior of scratch buffers owned by Nvim itself should follow what is recommended for plugins.\n\nMy (not very strong) opinion is similar to [this comment](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40336#issuecomment-4757303962). I.e. this should be handled by session save/restore mechanism and not by each plugin (scratch buffer owner) separately.",
