        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If a plugin provides URI buffers then only the plugin knows how to handle that URI. That is unrelated to the role of a session. The session saved the URI and that is all it should do, it shouldn't try to serialize the universe.\n\nThe implied purpose of a \"URI\" is that *the URI* has enough information to reproduce the content at any time. Like when you `:edit fugitive://...` or `:edit term://...` , the handlers for those URIs provide the relevant buffer contents. That is generally how URIs should work.",
